###Block: Copies and other lines
Charm Animal.COPY=Charm Animal (snakes and lizards only)

###Block: Descriptions
Eldritch Blast.MOD	DESC:Your eldritch blast is a ray of baleful magical energy that deals damage and other debilitating effects to your enemies. It deals (floor((CASTERLEVEL+1)/2))d6 points of damage (half damage to objects)
Baleful Utterance.MOD	DESC:You speak a single syllable of the Dark Speech that breaks brittle, nonmagical objects; sunders a single solid, nonmagical object; or damages a crystalline creature. If a creature is holding or wearing the target and it is destroyed, the creature must make a Fortitude save or be dazed for 1 round and deafened for 1 minute.
Beguiling Influence.MOD	DESC:You beguile and bewitch your foes and get a +6 bonus on Bluff, Diplomacy, and Intimidate checks.
Beshadowed Blast.MOD	DESC:Beshadowed blast renders the target blinded
Bewitching Blast.MOD	DESC:Bewitching Blast causes creatures struck to be confused, making them unable to independently determine what they will do.
Breath of the Night.MOD	DESC:A bank of fog billows out around you. The fog does not block line of sight but all creatures in the fog have concealment.
Brimstone Blast.MOD	DESC:Brimstone blast causes targets to catch on fire, taking 2d6 points of fire damage per round until it takes a full-round action to extinguish the flames or the duration expires.  A burning creature burning in this way never takes more than 2d6 points of fire damage in a round, even if it is hit by multiple brimstone blasts.
Chilling Tentacles.MOD	DESC:Conjures a field of soul chilling black tentacles, each 10 ft. long, which grapple all within 20 ft. spread. Creatures within the area take 2d6 points of cold damage each round whether or not they are grappled by the tentacles.
Curse of Despair.MOD	DESC:You place a curse on the subject.  -6 to an ability score; -4 on attack rolls, saves, and checks; or 50%% chance of losing each action. Even if the save against this ability succeeds, the creature takes -1 penalty on attack rolls for 1 minute.
Dark Discorporation.MOD	DESC:You become a swarm of Diminutive batlike shadows that fills two 10' squares or eight contiguous 5' squares, shapable as you desire. You gain the following traits: STR:1, Dex:+6, +4 size bonus to AC and +CHA mod deflection bonus, but lose natural and armor bonuses to AC. Fly speed 40' with perfect maneuverability and can pass through openings Diminutive creatures can pass. Swarm traits (see MM p.???), Swarm attack (strikes as magic weapon of your alignment) 4d6 damage to creatures in the space you occupy at end of turn. Distraction: creatures that begin their turn occupied by swarm must Fort save or be nauseated 1 round. Spellcasting requires concentration check. Possessions: gear becomes non-functional and is absorbed into your new form.  You can only take move actions while in this form - cannot use other invocations.
Dark Foresight.MOD	DESC:Grants you a powerful sixth sense in relation to yourself or another. Once foresight is cast, you receive instantaneous warnings of impending danger or harm to the subject of the spell. If you are within 100' and have line of sight you may communicate telepathically with the target.
Dark One's Own Luck.MOD	DESC:You are favored by the dark powers. You gain a luck bonus equal to your Charisma bonus on Fortitude saves, Reflex saves, or Will saves (your choice).  You can't apply this ability to two different save types at the same time.
Darkness (Invocation).MOD	DESC:Causes an object to radiate shadowy illumination out to a 20-ft. radius.
Dead Walk (The).MOD	DESC:Turn the bones and bodies of dead creatures into undead skeletons and zombies that obey your commands. Unless you include the normal material component for the spell (onyx gem worth 25 gp/HD of undead) as part of the process, undead created by this ability crumble into dust after (CASTERLEVEL) minutes.
Devil's Sight.MOD	DESC:You gain the visual acuity of a devil.  You can see normally in darkness and magical darkness up to 30 ft.
Devour Magic.MOD	DESC:You deliver greater dispel magic by touch and gain 5 temporary hit points for each spell level dispelled. These temporary hit points do not stack with other temporary hit points.  If a new spell is devoured you may replace the old temporary hit points with the new ones, thus resetting the clock.
Earthen Grasp (Invocation).MOD	DESC:You can cause an arm made of dense, compacted earth or soil (but not stone) to grapple your foes.  Treat as Medium creature with BAB +(CASTERLEVEL) and STR (floor(CASTERLEVEL/3)*2+14) the arm cannot move but can make one grapple attempt per round at any creature in it's or adjacent square. Each round it successfully pins a target it deals 1d6+STR lethal damage.  It has AC 15, hardness 4, (CASTERLEVEL*3) HP.
Eldritch Chain.MOD	DESC:You turn your eldritch blast into an arc of energy that jumps from the first target to others. All secondary targets must be within 30 ft. of the previous target and you can't target the same creature more than once.  You must make additional ranged touch attacks for each secondary target and if you miss any target in the chain, it ends there. Secondary blasts each deal full damage.
Eldritch Cone.MOD	DESC:Eldritch cone deals normal eldritch blast damage to all targets within the area.  No ranged touch attack is required but any creature in the area can attempt a saving throw.
Eldritch Doom.MOD	DESC:Eldritch doom deals normal eldritch blast damage to any targets designated by you within the area of effect. No ranged touch attack is required but any targeted creature in the area can attempt a saving throw.
Eldritch Spear.MOD	DESC:Eldritch spear increases the range of an eldritch blast attack to 250 feet with no range increment.
Enervating Shadow.MOD	DESC:The dark powers cloak you and shield you from harm while draining vitality from nearby foes.  You have total concealment in any area that isn't brightly lit.  Any creature adjacent to you takes a -4 penalty to STR for 5 rounds. Once affected, a creature cannot be affected again for 24 hours.  This invocation can be countered or dispelled by any light spell of equal or higher level.
Entropic Warding.MOD	DESC:Chaotic energies swirl about you, deflecting ranged attacks (arrows, rays, etc) to have 20%% miss chance. You can move through any type of terrain (mud, snow, dust, or the like) and leave neither footprints nor scent. Tracking you is impossible by nonmagical means.
Fell Flight.MOD	DESC:The powers of darkness bear you aloft as you sprout a streaming, winglike cape of shadows. You can fly at your land speed with good maneuverability.
Flee the Scene.MOD	DESC:You instantly transfer yourself from your current location to any other spot within range leaving behind a major image of yourself in your place that lasts for 1 round which reacts appropriately to attacks.
Frightful Blast.MOD	DESC:Creatures struck by frightful blast become shaken. A shaken creature struck by frightful blast is not affected by the shaken aspect of the blast but takes damage normally.
Hellrime Blast.MOD	DESC:Hellrime blast deals cold damage and any creature struck by the attack take a -4 penalty to Dexterity.  Dexterity penalties from multiple hellrime blasts do not stack.
Hideous Blow.MOD	DESC:A successful melee attack affects the target as if struck by your eldritch blast (including any eldritch essence applied to the blast) in addition to any weapon damage that you deal with the attack.
Hungry Darkness.MOD	DESC:This spell causes an object to radiate shadowy illumination out to a 20-ft. radius. Every square of this area is filled with a swarm of bats, which attacks all other creatures within its area.  If the bat swarm is destroyed, the darkness disappears as well.
Leaps and Bounds.MOD	DESC:You gain amazing agility and get a +6 bonus on Balance, Jump, and Tumble checks.
Miasmic Cloud.MOD	DESC:A misty cloud of fog spreads around you, which does not block line of sight, but all creatures in the fog have concealment.  Creatures who enter the fog become fatigued for as long as they remain within the cloud and 1 round thereafter.
Noxious Blast.MOD	DESC:Noxious blast causes creatures struck to become nauseated.
Path of Shadow.MOD	DESC:You and any creature you touch are then transported along a coiling path of shadowstuff to the edge of the Material Plane where it borders the Plane of Shadow.  In the region of shadow, you move at a rate of 50 miles per hour, moving normally on the borders of the Plane of Shadow but much more rapidly relative to the Material Plane. Thus, you can use this spell to travel rapidly by stepping onto the Plane of Shadow, moving the desired distance, and then stepping back onto the Material Plane. Each hour that you spend shadow walking you regain hit points as if you had rested for a full day.
Repelling Blast.MOD	DESC:Repelling Blast  causes any medium or smaller creature struck to be hurled 1d6X5 feet (1d6 squares) directly away from you and knocked prone. If the creature strikes a solid object they stop prematurely and take 1d6 points of damage per 10' hurled and still knocked prone.  Movement from the blast does not provoke attacks of opportunity.
Retributive Invisibility.MOD	DESC:You can use greater invisibility but if it is dispelled a shock wave releases from your body in a 20' radius burst dealing 4d6 points of sonic damage to all creatures and stuns them for one round. Fort save halves the damage and negates the stunning effect.
See the Unseen.MOD	DESC:You can see any objects or beings that are invisible within your range of vision, as well as any that are ethereal, as if they were normally visible. You also gain the ability to see up to 60 ft. in total darkness.
Sickening Blast.MOD	DESC:Creatures struck by sickening blast become sickened.  A sickened creature struck by a second sickening blast is not affected by the sickening aspect of the blast but still takes damage normally.
Spiderwalk.MOD	DESC:You can climb and travel on vertical surfaces or even traverse ceilings as well as a spider does. The affected creature must have its hands free to climb in this manner. You gain a climb speed of 20 feet; furthermore, it need not make Climb checks to traverse a vertical or horizontal surface (even upside down). You are unaffected by mundane or magical webs.
Stony Grasp (Invocation).MOD	DESC:You can cause an arm made of stone to appear from any natural surface to grapple your foes.  Treat as Medium creature with BAB +(CASTERLEVEL) and STR (floor(CASTERLEVEL/3)*2+14) the arm cannot move but can make one grapple attempt per round at any creature in it's or adjacent square. Each round it successfully pins a target it deals 1d6+STR lethal damage.  It has AC 18, hardness 8, (CASTERLEVEL*4) HP.
Summon Swarm (Invocation).MOD	DESC:You summon a swarm of bats, rats, or spiders (your choice), which attacks all other creatures within its area.
Tenacious Plague.MOD	DESC:You summon an insect plague but add Charisma modifier to Fort save to resist the distraction, attacks by the swarm are treated as magic weapons.
Utterdark Blast.MOD	DESC:Utterdark Blast deals negative energy damage and creatures struck gain two negative levels, which fade after 1 hour
Vitriolic Blast.MOD	DESC:Vitriolic Blast deals acid damage and 2d6 additional points of acid damage per round after the initial strike for the indicated duration.  This damage is not subject to spell resistance.
Voidsense.MOD	DESC:You can sharpen your hearing and sight, gaining blindsense out to 30 feet
Voracious Dispelling.MOD	DESC:Cancels magical spells and effects.  Any creature with an active spell effect that is dispelled takes 1 point of damage per level of the spell effect.
Walk Unseen.MOD	DESC:You become invisible, vanishing from sight, even from darkvision. If you are carrying gear, that vanishes, too.
Wall of Gloom (Invocation).MOD	DESC:Shadow barrier obscures vision and deters passage. Creatures in square adjacent to the wall have concealment against attacks from the other side, creatures more than 1 square away have total concealment.  Creatures with 6 or fewer HD must halt at its edge, ending its move action (though it can attempt to move through or away with a second move action). Each previous failure to pass the wall imposes a cumulative -1 penalty on its Will save. Wall of gloom counters or dispels any light spell of equal or lower level.
Wall of Perilous Flame.MOD	DESC:An immobile, blazing curtain of shimmering violet fire springs into existence. One side of the wall, selected by you, sends forth waves of heat, dealing 2d4 points of fire damage to creatures within 10 feet and 1d4 points of fire damage to those past 10 feet but within 20 feet. Half the damage is supernatural power and is therefore not subject to being reduced by resistance to fire.  If a creature is reduced to 0 HP or lower by the wall its remains are completely consumed 1 round later (as if by a destruction spell).
Warlock's Call.MOD	DESC:You contact a particular creature with which you are familiar and send a short message of twenty-five words or less to the subject. A creature unwilling to reply can attempt a Will save to turn the sending back on you, dealing 1d10 points of damage to you.
Word of Changing.MOD	DESC:You change the subject into a Small or smaller animal of nor more than 1 HD. 24 hours after being transformed the subject is entitled to a second saving throw (at its original bonus) to resume its normal form.  If failed it remains in the new form permanently.
Assay Resistance.MOD	DESC:+10 bonus on caster level checks to defeat one creature's spell resistance
Force Whip.MOD	DESC:Whip of magical force keeps animals at bay and can frighten animals as ranged touch attack
Imbue Familiar with Spell Ability.MOD	DESC:You transfer spells and casting ability into your familiar
Spirit Binding (Lesser).MOD	DESC:Traps spirit creature of 8 HD or less until it performs a task
Spirit Binding (Greater).MOD	DESC:As Spirit Binding (Lesser), but traps up to 24 HD of spirits
Superior Invisibility.MOD	DESC:Subject is invisible to sight, hearing and scent for 1 hour/level and can attack
Unluck.MOD	DESC:Target remakes all rolls, use worse result for 1 round/target

